@startuml 05-seq-convergence
!include _style.iuml
title Two peers edit concurrently and converge (WebSocket binding)

participant "MUPPET A\n(client 1, key P)" as a
participant "Host\n(branch main)" as t
participant "MUPPET B\n(client 2, key Q)" as b

note over a, b : Both start from the same state vector {1:7, 2:4}

par concurrent edits
  a -> a : set @fill="blue" on circle c1\nop (1,8)
  a -> t : update (1,8)
else
  b -> b : insert path p9 after c1\nop (2,5)
  b -> t : update (2,5)
end

t -> t : client 1 is bound to P,\nclient 2 to Q; both hold write.\nAdmit and record both.
t -> b : update (1,8)
b -> b : integrate (1,8)
t -> a : update (2,5)
a -> a : integrate (2,5)

note over a, b
  Both now at {1:8, 2:5}.
  Ops commute, so delivery order does not matter:
  the canonical XML (and its SHA-256) is identical.
end note
@enduml
